 its momentum so the  more i try to precisely determine where  this is at an instant as soon as i've  done that in the immediate aftermath of  that particle coming off its momentum is  completely uncertain i don't know which  direction it's scattered off this was  first enunciated by heisenberg so it's  known as heisenberg's uncertainty  principle and this idea of using a  microscope is heisenberg's microscope  and it's the idea that he came up with  way way back in 1927 after he'd invented  the mathematics that makes all this  clear people said that's obviously  nonsense and he kept  coming up with illustrations and people  tried to disprove his ideas but nobody  found a way around this

